{"reference":"Matthew 3","book":"Matthew","chapter":3,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Jesus’ Baptism","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Matthew presents Jesus’ baptism as a declaration of Spirit-marked sonship: the Spirit descends upon him and the heavenly voice names him God’s beloved Son. One interpretive reading sees this scene, together with the wilderness testing that follows, as framed by scriptural voices and Deuteronomy. Because that larger connection is disputed, it should be held as a way of reading Matthew’s presentation rather than as the chapter’s only possible meaning.","verse_refs":["Matthew 3:13-17"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_matthew_003_80a43731cc196a3b9ef9c3f8"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}